# exobios is a monorepo — the Vercel project's Root Directory is set to
# exobios-frontend, but a `vercel deploy` from the repo root still walks the
# whole tree to build the upload archive before applying that setting, and
# doesn't reliably respect nested .gitignore files in the other sub-projects
# (exobios-ai/.gitignore, exobios-backend/.gitignore). Without this, that
# walk picks up hundreds of MB of unrelated content — Python venvs, ingested
# textbook PDFs, Maven build output — and can exceed Vercel's 100MB
# single-file upload limit. Exclude the other sub-projects entirely; the
# frontend build never needs them.
exobios-ai/
exobios-backend/
